      "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_1",
      "label": "User projected onto the textual material via deictic reference",
      "description": "The user is projected onto the textual material 'text_chunk' because the phrase 'call me caitlyn' explicitly uses the deictic pronoun 'me', which directly addresses the viewer/user and maps them onto the identity being mocked. This creates a direct semiotic projection where the user is positioned as the speaker of the vulgar statement, thereby internalizing the abusive message. The spatial positioning of the text above the visual material reinforces this projection, making the user feel implicated in the act of speaking the insult.",
